A||||12||Slammed Fiero||CPU Cooling||||1||
Z||000000||Slammed Fiero||11-01-2001||08:02 PM||||I just put together my new computer. I built one last month , but it got pirated by my dad to his office.<P>In any case here is what I have:<P>T-Bird 1.2 Ghz Cpu Overclocked to 1.4<BR>Asus a7V motherboard with 266 FSB (DDR board)<BR>512 megs DDR ram<BR>Antec mid tower.<BR>GForce MX 64meg <BR>2 Compunurse 1 monitoring case temp , the other monitoring cpu temp , also have motherboard monitor installed to keep a closer eye on things.<P>Here's the tricky part , the CPu runs cool , I could overclock it more. Cooling the CPU is a thermaltake Dragon ORb 7000 ... IT's loud as hell!!!!!!! I need a fan that will give me the same sort of performance but quietier. last month a friend and I built a watercooling system for his setup , But I don't want to get that Advanced..yet.<P>Any ideas?<P>The monitor is a samsung flat screen ...it was worth the extra money. I'm running a copy of Windows XP.<P>I should have put this money into my car , but with the winter here I need something to modify!<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000001||SteveJ||11-01-2001||09:19 PM||||Want to see some processors burn up when the fan is removed?<BR> <A HREF="http://www6.tomshardware.com/cpu/01q3/010917/heatvideo-05.html#download_the_first_toms_hardware_test_lab_video" TARGET=_blank>http://www6.tomshardware.com/cpu/01q3/010917/heatvideo-05.html#download_the_first_toms_hardware_test_lab_video</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||grinthock||11-01-2001||09:36 PM||||Well, I have good AND bad news for ya.  The Golden orb's are actually only supposed to put out 20 CFM at 4500 RPM<P>The fan speed itself is faily middle of the road, tests show 2000-7000 rpm fans are out there, more speed usually equals more sound <P>The Golden orb puts out 48DB, which is middile for a fan. <P>Those golden orb numbers are from another site, Tom couldn't get orb's for some reason when he did the tests.  From other reviews I have seen they are all looks and no go, but some reviews love them!<P>The NoiseControl Silverado is probably what you want, there is a company here in Toronto who sells them, it has amazing performance and VERY quiet, 38DB (Consider 35DB is the baseline for ambient noise).<P>I put a noise control unit in a couple servers we had at the office in a demo room that customers were in, the room doubled as a boardroom and the room had a full vid/aud conference system in it I installed and we wanted the abient noise REAL low, so we used the noisecontrol units, they are WISPER quiet.  And have great performance.  Look for them.<BR> <A HREF="http://www6.tomshardware.com/cpu/01q1/010306/cooler-10.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www6.tomshardware.com/cpu/01q1/010306/cooler-10.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.plycon.com/silrado.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.plycon.com/silrado.htm</A> <P>Above is a nice link to look at it, yeah it's ugly, but it works.  it uses 50G of silver, silver has a VERY low resistance to heat transfer that is a reason for it's high performance.  <P>They are FAR from cheap, $40-60 USD I have seen them for, we picked some up for $65 Canadian from a company downtown.   Spadina and College.<P>Here is the web site with the lab tests.<BR> <A HREF="http://www4.tomshardware.com/cpu/01q2/010521/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www4.tomshardware.com/cpu/01q2/010521/index.html</A> <P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroworld.com</A>  The place to go for Fiero INFO! <BR>Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000003||grinthock||11-01-2001||09:38 PM||||the big USA dealer for NoiseControl (the official distributor) is<P> <A HREF="http://www.plycon.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.plycon.com/</A> <P><BR>The company I got them from doesn't carry them anymore they imported them from denmark or whereever they are made.  I might buy one from Plycon when noisecontrol releases one for the P4<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroworld.com</A>  The place to go for Fiero INFO! <BR>Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
