Z||000006||Slammed Fiero||11-01-2001||11:28 PM||||The RPM's are running right around 7020 , caries a bit. The fan looks cool , but it's too friggin loud. I have been looking at Koolance cpu coolers and perhasp making a watercooled setup. I have a few wisper quiet pumps that would work well.<P>Wow that is a friggin ugly duckling. But I'm in for 9 months of school and Don't know If I can stand 9 months of the Dragon orb's Buzz<P>I will have to post some pics..modding a computer is like hotrodding a car..very addictive.<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000007||grinthock||11-02-2001||06:46 AM||||You could go the water route, if you want my honest opinion, the best sound with the best performance at the best price is the stock Intel fan.  I am not talking some crap OEM fan, the actual INTEL fan that comes with a Boxed processor, they are super quiet and last a LONG time, it's the only one I've never had problems with (next to the noisecontrol)||||reg||1
Z||000008||Standard||11-02-2001||03:11 PM||||Sounds almost like my system..<BR>Tbird 1.2Ghz<BR>Abit KT7A-RAID<BR>256 mb ram<BR>Kyro II 64 mb<P>Have you 3dmarked it?  My highest score in 3dmark 2000 has been 6272 with it o/c to 1.4..   <A HREF="http://gamershq.madonion.com/compare.shtml?2101247" TARGET=_blank>http://gamershq.madonion.com/compare.shtml?2101247</A> <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000009||frontal lobe||11-02-2001||06:35 PM||||If you are going to spend that much on cooling, sell your 1.2 ghz cpu and just buy a 1.4 ghz cpu.  It will be cheaper.<P>I know, some people just like to overclock.<P>Standard, I thought kyro's didn't benchmark that well, for some reason.<P>My cheapo geforce 2 mx on an abit kt7a raid (not using the raid), 1 ghz/200 athlon, 256 ram gives me only 4800 on 3dmark 2000.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Slammed Fiero||11-02-2001||06:40 PM||||I wanted to get the system built fast The 1.2 is what they had on hand. I bought a good mother board and when the time comes I will upgrade the processor. I bought another 256Mb DDR ram today.<P>I broke down and ordered a Silverado last night as per grinthocks suggestion , Should be here next week hopefully.<P>I think my next Big upgrade would be a dual processor setup , but i have been hearing that there are some glitches with such setups thus far. Plus It's hard to find an intelligent person to talk to about it. Most think that 2  1.2 Ghz processors  equals 2.4ghz's of power. (Dumbasses)<P>All this money could be going into my car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Ohh well Car won't see much use next summer so May as well direct my fundage other places.<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000011||grinthock||11-02-2001||08:09 PM||||Multiple processors, let's start another thread on this.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Standard||11-02-2001||10:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by frontal lobe:<BR><B>Standard, I thought kyro's didn't benchmark that well, for some reason.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Kyro's don't benchmark good, mainly in 3dmark.  3dmark is very dependent on hardware transformation & lighting, which the Kyro doesn't have.   If I had a geforce based card I'd probably be benching in the 7-8,000 range.  But 3dmark is a synthetic benchmark, doesn't necessarily mean much in the real world.  Also, kyro performance doesn't really decrease as you go up in resolution and color depth.  I run my games in 1024x768 at 32 bit.  Sometimes at 1280x1024.  I average 80+ FPS in quake III.||||reg||1
